## Architecture Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
|----------|--------|-----------|
| Storage | In-memory array | Zero dependencies, instant setup, easy to understand. Swap the model for a DB later without changing routes. |
| Error handling | Custom classes + centralized middleware | Consistent error responses, automatic status codes, clean separation of concerns. |
| Async/await | Used in all route handlers | Ready for async data layers; cleaner than `.then()` chains; Express handles errors automatically. |
| PUT vs PATCH | Full replacement (PUT) | Simpler validation — all fields required. PATCH would require partial-update logic. |
| Route organization | Separate router module | Scalable — new resources get their own files without cluttering app.js. |

