# 📚 Book REST API

An educational REST API built with **Node.js** and **Express.js** that manages a collection of books using in-memory storage. Every line of code is documented to explain the "why" behind each design decision.

## 🚀 Quick Start

### Prerequisites
- Node.js 18+ installed
- npm or yarn package manager

### Installation & Running

```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
npm install

# 2. Start the server (development mode with auto-reload)
npm run dev

# Or for production:
npm start
```

The API will be available at **http://localhost:5000**

## 📖 API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint          | Description                      |
|--------|-------------------|----------------------------------|
| GET    | `/`               | API info & endpoint listing      |
| GET    | `/books`          | List all books (with filtering)  |
| GET    | `/books/stats`    | Aggregate statistics             |
| GET    | `/books/:id`      | Get a single book by ID          |
| POST   | `/books`          | Create a new book                |
| PUT    | `/books/:id`      | Full update an existing book     |
| DELETE | `/books/:id`      | Delete a book by ID              |

## 🧪 Testing the API

### Get all books
```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/books
```

### Filter books by genre
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/books?genre=Fiction"
```

### Filter books by year range
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/books?yearFrom=1950&yearTo=2000"
```

### Get a single book
```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/books/1
```

### Create a new book
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/books \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "The Catcher in the Rye",
    "author": "J.D. Salinger",
    "year": 1951,
    "genre": "Fiction"
  }'
```

### Update a book (full replacement)
```bash
curl -X PUT http://localhost:5000/books/1 \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "To Kill a Mockingbird (Updated Edition)",
    "author": "Harper Lee",
    "year": 1960,
    "genre": "Fiction"
  }'
```

### Delete a book
```bash
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:5000/books/3
```

### Get statistics
```bash
curl http://localhost:5000/books/stats
```

